WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.950
Cambridge English readers start a level.

00:04.000 --> 00:05.950
Why?

00:06.000 --> 00:07.950
Bifillip Mouse

00:08.000 --> 00:12.000
Published by Cambridge University Press.

00:24.000 --> 00:25.950
Why?

00:26.000 --> 00:28.000
Bifillip Mouse

00:30.000 --> 00:32.000
Bifillip Mouse

00:39.000 --> 00:40.950
Chapter 1

00:41.000 --> 00:43.000
Goodbye.

00:44.000 --> 00:48.950
Please don't go to Glossia. Says Sara.

00:49.000 --> 00:51.950
You're only 19.

00:52.000 --> 00:57.950
Alex is saying goodbye to Sara, his girlfriend.

00:58.000 --> 01:01.950
I must. Answer Alex.

01:02.000 --> 01:03.950
I'm a soldier.

01:04.000 --> 01:05.950
It's my job.

01:06.000 --> 01:08.950
I must go where the army says.

01:09.000 --> 01:14.950
But why are you going there? Ask Sara.

01:15.000 --> 01:19.950
We're going to stop the fighting. Says Alex.

01:20.000 --> 01:22.950
Lots of people are dying.

01:23.000 --> 01:28.950
But why are they fighting? Ask Sara.

01:29.000 --> 01:32.950
I don't know. Answer Alex.

01:33.000 --> 01:36.950
Why don't you ask? Says Sara.

01:37.000 --> 01:39.950
You never ask questions.

01:40.000 --> 01:43.950
I know. Answer Alex.

01:44.000 --> 01:45.950
I'm sorry.

01:46.000 --> 01:47.950
I hate asking questions.

01:48.000 --> 01:52.950
Please change Alex. Says Sara.

01:53.000 --> 01:55.000
For me.

01:56.000 --> 02:00.950
I'm going to think about you every day. Says Sara.

02:01.000 --> 02:02.950
Me too.

02:03.000 --> 02:04.950
Alex answers.

02:05.000 --> 02:07.950
I can send you a text from my phone tomorrow.

02:08.000 --> 02:10.950
And I think there's email.

02:11.000 --> 02:12.950
That's good.

02:13.000 --> 02:15.950
Sara says with a little smile.

02:16.000 --> 02:18.950
I love you, Alex.

02:19.000 --> 02:22.950
And I love you too. Answer Alex.

02:23.000 --> 02:30.950
Now, don't be sad.

02:31.000 --> 02:32.950
Chapter 2.

02:33.000 --> 02:35.950
We're in glossia now.

02:36.000 --> 02:39.950
Alex is on the plane to glossia.

02:40.000 --> 02:42.950
He's sitting next to Sergeant Ken.

02:43.000 --> 02:48.000
It's Ken's second time in glossia.

02:49.000 --> 02:50.950
Excuse me, Sergeant.

02:51.000 --> 02:52.950
Alex starts.

02:53.000 --> 02:57.950
You can call me Ken. The Sergeant says.

02:58.000 --> 03:03.950
Why are they fighting in glossia? Alex asks.

03:04.000 --> 03:09.950
That's not an easy question. Ken answers.

03:10.000 --> 03:12.950
I think it's like this.

03:13.000 --> 03:15.950
Some people have guns.

03:16.000 --> 03:19.950
They use the guns because they want something.

03:20.000 --> 03:24.950
Then other people get guns to fight back with.

03:25.000 --> 03:27.950
Now everyone has guns.

03:28.000 --> 03:32.950
And everyone forgets what they are fighting about.

03:33.000 --> 03:35.950
But where do the guns come from?

03:36.000 --> 03:38.950
Is Alex's next question?

03:39.000 --> 03:46.950
People from other countries sell them to the glossions. Ken answers.

03:47.000 --> 03:49.950
Why? asks Alex.

03:50.000 --> 03:52.950
Ken smiles.

03:53.000 --> 03:53.950
Money.

03:54.000 --> 03:55.950
That's why.

03:56.000 --> 04:02.950
Ken, can we stop people buying and selling guns? Alex asks.

04:03.000 --> 04:04.950
No, we can't.

04:05.000 --> 04:10.950
The people who sell the guns, they're thousands of kilometers away.

04:11.000 --> 04:15.950
All we can do is help the people here in this country.

04:16.000 --> 04:18.950
Answers, Ken.

04:19.000 --> 04:23.950
We're going to a famous old town called Tonic.

04:24.000 --> 04:28.950
In Tonic, lots of people are fighting each other.

04:29.000 --> 04:33.950
And some of them are also fighting us.

04:34.000 --> 04:39.950
There's a very loud noise, and the plane goes over to the right.

04:40.000 --> 04:43.950
What's that? Shouts Alex.

04:44.000 --> 04:45.950
What do you think?

04:46.000 --> 04:47.950
Answers, Ken.

04:48.000 --> 04:51.950
We're in glossier now.

04:52.000 --> 04:55.950
Is it always like this? Alex asks.

04:56.000 --> 04:58.950
Yes? Ken answers.

04:59.000 --> 05:03.950
But the papers say the glossion people want us here.

05:04.000 --> 05:05.950
Alex says.

05:06.000 --> 05:08.950
The sergeant smiles.

05:09.000 --> 05:12.950
Some glossions do, and some don't.

05:13.000 --> 05:14.950
Answers, Ken.

05:15.000 --> 05:18.950
But we're here to help all the people.

05:19.000 --> 05:23.950
And is it always hot? asks Alex.

05:24.000 --> 05:25.950
Yes.

05:26.000 --> 05:28.000
Laughs, Ken.

05:32.000 --> 05:33.950
Chapter 3.

05:34.000 --> 05:37.950
Soldiers get out.

05:38.000 --> 05:41.950
Sergeant Ken and Alex drive into Tonic.

05:42.000 --> 05:44.950
People watch them.

05:45.000 --> 05:52.950
Alex, this is where you're living for the next six months, says Ken.

05:53.000 --> 05:58.950
Your bed's over there, and this is Hawk.

05:59.000 --> 06:05.950
A tall man with very short hair stands up and puts out his hand.

06:06.000 --> 06:08.950
Hi. He says.

06:09.000 --> 06:11.950
Ah, that's Stefan on the bed.

06:12.000 --> 06:13.950
Ken says.

06:14.000 --> 06:17.950
Stefan smiles at Alex.

06:18.000 --> 06:18.950
Hello?

06:19.000 --> 06:22.950
Put your things down. He says.

06:23.000 --> 06:25.950
Do you want something to eat or drink?

06:26.000 --> 06:27.950
Yes, please.

06:28.000 --> 06:29.950
Answers, Alex.

06:30.000 --> 06:31.950
I'm going now.

06:32.000 --> 06:33.950
Ken says.

06:34.000 --> 06:35.950
You must be tired, Alex.

06:36.000 --> 06:38.950
Try and get some sleep tonight.

06:39.000 --> 06:42.950
We start work in the morning.

06:43.000 --> 06:44.950
Hi, Sarah.

06:45.000 --> 06:47.950
It's very hot in glossia.

06:48.000 --> 06:51.950
Sergeant Ken says we're here to help.

06:52.000 --> 06:53.950
But can we?

06:54.000 --> 06:56.950
I don't know.

06:57.000 --> 07:00.000
All my love, Alex.

07:05.000 --> 07:06.950
Chapter 4.

07:07.000 --> 07:09.950
First Patrol.

07:10.000 --> 07:14.950
The next day, it's time for Alex's first patrol.

07:15.000 --> 07:17.950
Just do what I do.

07:18.000 --> 07:19.950
Ken tells Alex.

07:20.000 --> 07:24.950
Stefan and Hawk are going to walk behind us.

07:25.000 --> 07:29.950
Use your eyes and ears and look everywhere.

07:30.000 --> 07:36.950
And don't forget, we never know who is a friend and who isn't.

07:37.000 --> 07:42.950
What are we looking for? Ask Alex.

07:43.000 --> 07:44.950
Gums.

07:45.000 --> 07:47.950
Answers, Ken, with a quick laugh.

07:48.000 --> 07:49.950
And gunman.

07:50.000 --> 07:51.950
Hawk says.

07:52.000 --> 07:54.950
He isn't laughing.

07:55.000 --> 08:00.950
But what about the people who sell the guns? Alex asks.

08:01.000 --> 08:02.950
They're not here.

08:03.000 --> 08:04.950
Hawk answers.

08:05.000 --> 08:09.950
They're far away with their money.

08:10.000 --> 08:13.950
Some people are happy to see the soldiers.

08:14.000 --> 08:16.950
They stop and say hello.

08:17.000 --> 08:21.950
But some boys aren't happy that the soldiers are there.

08:22.000 --> 08:25.950
They're throwing things at the patrol and shouting.

08:26.000 --> 08:31.950
The soldiers don't understand what the boys are shouting.

08:32.000 --> 08:34.950
Something hits Alex in the mouth.

08:35.000 --> 08:37.950
He turns with his gun.

08:38.000 --> 08:42.950
Alex isn't slow, but the boys are very fast.

08:43.000 --> 08:44.950
They run away.

08:45.000 --> 08:47.950
Alex feels his mouth.

08:48.000 --> 08:49.950
Are you okay?

08:50.000 --> 08:51.950
Stefan shouts.

08:52.000 --> 08:53.950
Yes!

08:54.000 --> 08:55.950
Answers, Alex.

08:56.000 --> 08:58.950
Then they hear a gun.

08:59.000 --> 09:02.950
Someone's shooting at them.

09:03.000 --> 09:07.950
Alex looks across the dirty street at a house.

09:08.000 --> 09:12.950
He sees someone at a bedroom window.

09:13.000 --> 09:13.950
Look!

09:14.000 --> 09:14.950
Up there!

09:15.000 --> 09:16.950
Alex shouts.

09:17.000 --> 09:21.950
Hawk turns, looks up, and shoots at the window.

09:22.000 --> 09:26.950
Ken and Alex run across the street to the house.

09:27.000 --> 09:31.950
They open the front door and run up to the bedroom.

09:32.000 --> 09:36.950
Hawk and Stefan wait in the street.

09:37.000 --> 09:38.950
Hi, Sarah.

09:39.000 --> 09:40.950
What a bad day.

09:41.000 --> 09:43.950
My first patrol.

09:44.000 --> 09:48.950
There's shooting, and I see someone at a bedroom window.

09:49.000 --> 09:51.950
Hawk shoots at the window.

09:52.000 --> 09:56.950
Then Ken and I run into the house and up to the bedroom.

09:57.000 --> 09:59.950
But there isn't a gunman there.

10:00.000 --> 10:02.950
It's a little boy.

10:03.000 --> 10:06.950
The boy's mother comes and shouts at us.

10:07.000 --> 10:13.000
I don't understand what she's saying, but I can see she's very angry.

10:14.000 --> 10:18.950
I want to say sorry, but I don't speak glossion.

10:19.000 --> 10:24.950
When we leave, the woman is shouting and the small boy is crying.

10:25.000 --> 10:26.950
I don't feel well.

10:27.000 --> 10:28.950
It's all wrong.

10:29.000 --> 10:31.950
What am I doing here?

10:32.000 --> 10:39.950
All my love, Alex.

10:40.000 --> 10:44.950
Chapter 5. We have no names.

10:45.000 --> 10:52.950
The next day, Sergeant Ken, Alex, Hawk, and Stefan are on patrol again.

10:53.000 --> 10:55.950
It's 12 o'clock.

10:56.000 --> 11:00.950
A kilometer away, a family is finishing lunch.

11:01.000 --> 11:08.950
There's a 12-year-old boy called Happy and an 8-year-old girl called Marina.

11:09.000 --> 11:13.950
Their mother's name is Ada, and she's very beautiful.

11:14.000 --> 11:16.950
There's no father.

11:17.000 --> 11:19.950
He's dead.

11:20.000 --> 11:25.950
In the afternoon, Ada puts away the lunch things and makes coffee.

11:26.000 --> 11:31.950
Happy is sitting on the floor in the living room with Marina.

11:32.000 --> 11:36.950
The brother and sister are laughing and playing with a doll.

11:37.000 --> 11:40.950
Ada doesn't hear the back door.

11:41.000 --> 11:42.950
Two men come in.

11:43.000 --> 11:46.950
One is tall and one is short.

11:47.000 --> 11:49.950
The short man has a bag.

11:50.000 --> 11:57.950
They're wearing white t-shirts and black trousers, and they have black masks.

11:58.000 --> 12:00.950
Ada looks at the two men.

12:01.000 --> 12:06.950
Then she shouts to her children, come here now!

12:07.000 --> 12:11.950
Happy and Marina run to their mother and stand by her.

12:12.000 --> 12:15.950
They're afraid of the two men in masks.

12:16.000 --> 12:18.950
Who are you?

12:19.000 --> 12:21.950
Ada asks the men.

12:22.000 --> 12:23.950
They don't answer.

12:24.000 --> 12:30.950
The short man puts the bag down, and the tall man looks at Ada.

12:31.000 --> 12:35.950
What are your names? asks Ada.

12:36.000 --> 12:41.950
We have no names, and we have no faces.

12:42.000 --> 12:44.950
Answers the tall man.

12:45.000 --> 12:47.950
We are not rich.

12:48.000 --> 12:52.950
What do you want? asks Ada.

12:53.000 --> 12:57.950
Nothing answers the short man.

12:58.000 --> 13:07.950
All we want is your house for ten minutes.

13:08.000 --> 13:09.950
Chapter 6

13:10.000 --> 13:14.000
Don't ask stupid questions.

13:15.000 --> 13:19.950
A young woman with a baby comes in the front door.

13:20.000 --> 13:23.950
Who's she? asks Ada.

13:24.000 --> 13:27.950
Shh, says the tall man.

13:28.000 --> 13:30.950
The baby.

13:31.000 --> 13:33.950
The young woman takes up the baby.

13:34.000 --> 13:35.950
It's sleeping.

13:36.000 --> 13:40.950
Under the baby is a long gun.

13:41.000 --> 13:46.950
The tall man takes the gun, and the woman puts the baby down again.

13:47.000 --> 13:52.950
What are you going to do? asks Happy.

13:53.000 --> 13:58.950
A soldier's going to die. Answers the short man.

13:59.000 --> 14:02.950
Why? asks Happy.

14:03.000 --> 14:08.950
Don't ask stupid questions, says the tall man.

14:09.000 --> 14:11.950
This is our country.

14:12.000 --> 14:17.950
We don't want soldiers from other countries here.

14:18.000 --> 14:21.950
You, the short man shouts to Marina.

14:22.000 --> 14:25.950
Give me your doll.

14:26.000 --> 14:27.950
Do it!

14:28.000 --> 14:30.950
Ada tells her daughter.

14:31.000 --> 14:33.950
Marina gives the man her doll.

14:34.000 --> 14:39.950
He takes something out of his bag and puts it in the doll.

14:40.000 --> 14:45.950
Then he takes a phone and puts it in the doll too.

14:46.000 --> 14:48.950
Listen, you too.

14:49.000 --> 14:51.950
The short man tells the children.

14:52.000 --> 14:54.950
You mustn't play with the doll now.

14:55.000 --> 14:57.950
Do you understand?

14:58.000 --> 14:59.950
Yes!

15:00.000 --> 15:01.950
Happy answers.

15:02.000 --> 15:07.950
Here, the short man says to the young woman with the baby.

15:08.000 --> 15:13.950
Take the doll and leave it in the street in front of the house.

15:14.000 --> 15:18.950
The short man speaks to the children.

15:19.000 --> 15:22.950
Go and play in front of the house now.

15:23.000 --> 15:28.950
But when you see the soldiers, you must run in again.

15:29.000 --> 15:30.950
He looks at Ada.

15:31.000 --> 15:37.950
Then you take your children out of the house by the back door.

15:38.000 --> 15:39.950
Do you understand?

15:40.000 --> 15:43.950
Yes! Says Ada.

15:44.000 --> 15:46.950
Happy and Marina.

15:47.000 --> 15:50.950
Go out and play in the street now.

15:51.000 --> 15:55.000
But don't go near the doll.

15:56.000 --> 15:59.950
The short man gives a phone to the tall man.

16:00.000 --> 16:06.950
This phone's for you, and there's a phone in the doll. He says.

16:07.000 --> 16:12.950
The tall man takes the gun and the phone up to the bedroom.

16:13.000 --> 16:16.950
The young woman goes with him.

16:17.000 --> 16:21.950
Out of the window, they can see the children in the street.

16:22.000 --> 16:24.950
And the doll.

16:25.000 --> 16:29.950
The tall man has the phone in his hand.

16:30.000 --> 16:35.950
All we can do now is await, he tells the woman.

16:36.000 --> 16:37.950
Listen!

16:38.000 --> 16:41.950
What's that? asks the woman.

16:42.000 --> 16:43.950
Can you hear something?

16:44.000 --> 16:47.950
Yes, the tall man answers.

16:48.000 --> 16:49.950
It's the soldiers.

16:50.000 --> 16:56.950
They're coming.

16:57.000 --> 16:58.950
Chapter 7.

16:59.000 --> 17:01.950
They're afraid of us.

17:02.000 --> 17:04.950
Why are the children running away?

17:05.000 --> 17:07.950
Alex asks Hawk.

17:08.000 --> 17:10.950
Because they're afraid of us!

17:11.000 --> 17:12.950
Hawk answers.

17:13.000 --> 17:14.950
But why?

17:15.000 --> 17:17.950
Alex, we're here to help.

17:18.000 --> 17:21.950
Don't they know that we're their friends?

17:22.000 --> 17:25.950
The patrol gets near to Ada's house.

17:26.000 --> 17:27.950
Yes!

17:28.000 --> 17:30.950
The children must be afraid of us.

17:31.000 --> 17:33.950
Alex says to Hawk.

17:34.000 --> 17:34.950
Look!

17:35.000 --> 17:37.950
That's their doll in the street.

17:38.000 --> 17:39.950
I'm going to give it to them.

17:40.000 --> 17:44.000
Then they can see we're their friends.

17:45.000 --> 17:48.000
Alex runs over to the doll.

17:49.000 --> 17:52.950
Stop! Shouts Ken.

17:53.000 --> 17:54.950
Alex looks up.

17:55.000 --> 17:57.950
Why? He asks.

17:58.000 --> 18:00.950
I'm just trying to help.

18:01.000 --> 18:04.950
Do what I say! Shouts Ken.

18:05.000 --> 18:07.950
Come here now!

18:08.000 --> 18:13.000
Up in the bedroom, the tall man speaks to the young woman.

18:14.000 --> 18:17.950
The phone isn't working!

18:18.000 --> 18:20.950
He's very angry.

18:21.000 --> 18:23.950
What about the gun?

18:24.000 --> 18:26.950
The young woman asks.

18:27.000 --> 18:29.950
The tall man looks at Hawk.

18:30.000 --> 18:31.950
Then it's Stefan.

18:32.000 --> 18:34.950
Then Sergeant Ken.

18:35.000 --> 18:39.950
Then he looks at Alex and chooses.

18:40.000 --> 18:45.950
You're going to die, he says.

18:46.000 --> 18:48.950
The tall man shoots.

18:49.000 --> 18:53.950
Alex's mouth opens and he tries to say something.

18:54.000 --> 18:57.950
Then his eyes close.

18:58.000 --> 19:00.950
He doesn't say anything.

19:01.000 --> 19:03.950
He doesn't see anything.

19:04.000 --> 19:06.950
He doesn't feel anything.

19:07.000 --> 19:09.950
He's dead.

19:10.000 --> 19:12.950
Hawk turns and looks up.

19:13.000 --> 19:17.950
He sees someone at the bedroom window.

19:18.000 --> 19:19.950
Up there!

19:20.000 --> 19:23.950
Hawk shouts and shoots.

19:24.000 --> 19:29.950
Then Ken and Stefan shoot at the window.

19:30.000 --> 19:36.000
The young woman helps the tall man down to the living room.

19:37.000 --> 19:38.950
Here!

19:39.000 --> 19:40.950
Quick!

19:41.000 --> 19:42.950
Take the gun!

19:43.000 --> 19:45.950
He says to the young woman.

19:46.000 --> 19:50.950
She takes the gun and puts it under the baby.

19:51.000 --> 19:52.950
Come on!

19:53.000 --> 19:56.950
The soldiers are coming! Shouts the short man.

19:57.000 --> 20:00.950
You must see a doctor!

20:01.000 --> 20:04.950
I can't go anywhere!

20:05.000 --> 20:06.950
The tall man says.

20:07.000 --> 20:08.950
You two go!

20:09.000 --> 20:11.950
Now!

20:12.000 --> 20:19.950
He closes his eyes.

20:20.000 --> 20:21.950
Chapter 8.

20:22.000 --> 20:25.950
Don't say anything.

20:26.000 --> 20:31.950
The young woman and the short man run out of the back of the house.

20:32.000 --> 20:36.950
Ada and the children are waiting there.

20:37.000 --> 20:38.950
Where's your friend?

20:39.000 --> 20:41.950
Ada asks.

20:42.000 --> 20:42.950
Dead.

20:43.000 --> 20:45.950
The young woman answers.

20:46.000 --> 20:49.950
Why? Asks happy.

20:50.000 --> 20:52.950
Because of the soldiers.

20:53.000 --> 20:55.950
The young woman says.

20:56.000 --> 21:00.950
She turns and walks away fast with the baby.

21:01.000 --> 21:03.950
I hate soldiers.

21:04.000 --> 21:05.950
Happy says.

21:06.000 --> 21:09.950
Don't tell the soldiers about us.

21:10.000 --> 21:12.950
The short man tells Ada.

21:13.000 --> 21:18.950
He takes off his mask and she can see his face now.

21:19.000 --> 21:21.950
And your boy's coming with me.

21:22.000 --> 21:27.950
Don't say anything to the soldiers or he dies.

21:28.000 --> 21:31.950
He takes happy's hand and starts to run off.

21:32.000 --> 21:35.950
No! Shouts Ada.

21:36.000 --> 21:37.950
Don't take him!

21:38.000 --> 21:39.950
Happy!

21:40.000 --> 21:45.950
Ken, Hawk and Stefan run in the front door of the house.

21:46.000 --> 21:48.950
They see the dead man in the living room.

21:49.000 --> 21:51.950
Stefan runs up to the bedroom.

21:52.000 --> 21:56.950
Hawk and Ken go out to the back of the house.

21:57.000 --> 22:00.950
They find Ada and Marina there.

22:01.000 --> 22:04.950
Hawk speaks a little glossion.

22:05.000 --> 22:06.950
Where are they?

22:07.000 --> 22:08.950
He shouts.

22:09.000 --> 22:11.950
Ada says nothing.

22:12.000 --> 22:15.950
Then Hawk sees two people running away.

22:16.000 --> 22:18.950
A man and a boy.

22:19.000 --> 22:21.950
Hawk doesn't wait.

22:22.000 --> 22:23.950
He shoots.

22:24.000 --> 22:25.950
No!

22:26.000 --> 22:28.950
Ada shouts.

22:29.000 --> 22:34.950
Ken takes Ada and Marina into the house.

22:35.000 --> 22:42.950
Half an hour later, two kilometers away, the young woman is walking with the baby.

22:43.000 --> 22:47.950
Two soldiers see her and ask her to stop.

22:48.000 --> 22:52.950
Where are you going? asks one of the soldiers.

22:53.000 --> 22:56.950
To the shops. Answers the woman.

22:57.000 --> 23:00.950
I'm going to buy some food.

23:01.000 --> 23:03.950
She smiles at the soldiers.

23:04.000 --> 23:05.950
What's in there?

23:06.000 --> 23:07.950
The soldier shouts.

23:08.000 --> 23:09.950
My baby.

23:10.000 --> 23:11.950
The woman says.

23:12.000 --> 23:13.950
Please don't shout.

23:14.000 --> 23:16.950
He's sleeping.

23:17.000 --> 23:19.950
She smiles again.

23:20.000 --> 23:22.950
Okay. You can go.

23:23.000 --> 23:32.950
Says one of the soldiers and smiles at her.

23:33.000 --> 23:34.950
Chapter 9.

23:35.000 --> 23:36.950
Why?

23:37.000 --> 23:41.950
There are lots of soldiers at Ada's house now.

23:42.000 --> 23:46.950
They take Alex and the tall man away in a car.

23:47.000 --> 23:50.950
A glossy man is helping Sergeant Ken.

23:51.000 --> 23:54.950
He's asking Ada lots of questions.

23:55.000 --> 23:58.950
But Ada doesn't answer.

23:59.000 --> 24:02.950
All she can think of is happy.

24:03.000 --> 24:04.950
Where is he?

24:05.000 --> 24:06.950
Is he dead?

24:07.000 --> 24:11.950
She takes Marina's hand and listens to the questions.

24:12.000 --> 24:14.950
But she doesn't answer.

24:15.000 --> 24:19.950
The soldiers leave Ada and Marina in the house.

24:20.000 --> 24:24.950
That evening Ada hears a noise at the back door.

24:25.000 --> 24:26.950
It's dark.

24:27.000 --> 24:31.950
She opens the door and sees happy there.

24:32.000 --> 24:36.950
Are the soldiers here? asks happy.

24:37.000 --> 24:38.950
No.

24:39.000 --> 24:43.950
Ada says with a big smile and takes happy in her arms.

24:44.000 --> 24:53.950
Alex, why don't you answer my emails?

24:54.000 --> 24:55.950
Are you okay?

24:56.000 --> 24:58.950
Why don't you write?

24:59.000 --> 25:00.950
Why?

25:01.000 --> 25:02.950
Why?

25:03.000 --> 25:04.950
All my love.

25:05.000 --> 25:08.000
Sara.
